    "rationale": [
      "The compiler has a typed public contract, deterministic producer, replayable writer, audit surface, Fabric/source-contract consumers, runtime-quality consumers, and unit/integration tests.",
      "It is not route-pinned because the normal catalog resolve -> FetchPlan -> FetchExecutor path does not consume DataRequirementSpec rows or source-contract binding status before connector.fetch.",
      "It is not out_of_route because it governs the same data admissibility seam and is consumed by scenario contracts, production-data contract index, Fabric requirement binding, and producer pipeline code.",
      "It is not pure built_not_wired because consumers exist; the missing bridge is specifically from compiler/contract binding into pinned fetch admission and public GY census coverage."
    ]
